hey what's up my name is samuel lees and  in this video i am going to share with  you why i am not doing this deal anymore  i was about to buy a property a project  development opportunity in  just outside of warsaw and i've talked  about this i've been talking about it  for the last couple of days at some of  my events however  something happened due diligence  happened and i decided to walk away from  the deal now i really really believe  that in property investment sometimes  knowing what not to do is as important  as knowing what to do because knowing  when to walk away is just as important  as being told to take action and to step  in so i had a property opportunity  someone actually at one of my courses  i've been running a crash course tour  someone um who i know trusted friend  that was at the crash course tour  pitched me on an idea of buying a pub  conversion just outside of warsaw and  i'm from warsaw so i'm like yeah man i  love the idea and um you know he showed  me the numbers he gave me a due  diligence  sheet and i paid  this person who is a friend and you know  a good property investor i paid them a 5  000 pound finders fee for this pub  conversion and the figures were as  follows he had negotiated to buy the pub  for 125  000 pounds i'm like cool  the pub already had planning permission  in place to turn to 12 apartments it was  going to cost apparently around about  400 000 pounds to turn it to 12  apartments i'm like okay great and that  means 400 grand in 125 you're talking  about 525 000 pounds all in am i going  to use my money of course not i'm going  to get um bridging finance or  development finance so i'm going to pull  in private investment onto the deal so  i'll put a little bit of my money in so  that was the deal 525 all in and then  the end value was 800 000 pounds once  all the apartments were done and  finished so you know there was about 275  000 pounds profit so the deal seemed  okay so what is the net percentage  profit on that deal and he'd done all  his due diligence so  uh if the end value was  800  800 000  which he said would be conservative  times point two five minus two hundred  thousand it's going to leave you six  hundred thousand so it's a good deal it  makes it stacked so i'm like you know  what it sounds really good so i paid a 5  000 pound finder's fee um  and that was that however  something happens and this is what i  started to walk out so firstly i  calculated the gross development value  i.e the end value of the property and i  think 800 000 was a little bit  optimistic so when i looked at it i did  some comparables now this pub by the way  he'd done the comparables by saying look  there's these apartments there's these  apartments that were selling for um  x amount which  so it was you know the due diligence was  done the problem was this pub was in a  slightly rough part of town sometimes  you can have a road  and one end of the road the house prices  or the apartment prices can be more than  the other end of the road so first  lesson is know your area know your patch  so when i looked at the the property of  the pub i'm like  i don't think the end value is going to  be 800 000 pounds i think it's going to  be more like 700 000 pounds so straight  away you've most of your profits gone  just on miscalculating the end value  however what gets worse  is when i sent the estimations to my  brother  ben machakanyanga he looked at the  property and he also said that he  thought that the um the cost of refurb  costs have gone up a lot the prices of  building which is going to block he  thought that that was a little bit low  only about eight or nine percent wrong  but the thing is if you're  10 wrong on your gtv and 10 wrong on  your co  on your refurb costs i mean that could  you could be 20 out well your profit  might be 20  so that means  you could potentially be making zero  money and then you're just refurbing a  pub for fun but you're not going to make  any money it doesn't make sense so this  deal looked great on paper but after  doing serious due diligence um it ended  up it wasn't actually a good deal at all  so i told my friend and he refunded me  the five thousand pound finders fee i  was within my 14 day due diligence  calling off period and now i'm not doing  the pub anymore i'm really disappointed  because i've talked about it i've been  sharing about oh i've just bought this  uh i've just played this funny i'm about  to buy this pub um but i'm not doing it  anymore so if anyone's heard the story  about this pub this is what's gone wrong  this is what's happened however  i actually think if i bought it and if i  did it up and if i you know i could even  vlog it or if i shared the success with  my students i actually think that you're  probably gonna learn more from what  didn't happen and what went wrong than  if it actually went successful and went  ahead there's so many lessons in this um  let me know in the comment box what do  you think the key lessons are from this  deal i think number one the first lesson  is um always make sure that you use your  formulas not your feelings when emotions  are high intelligence is low i wanted to  go ahead with this deal because i knew  the pub  i grew up in warsaw and i genuinely just  wanted to restore it but i needed to  remember that this isn't about what i  want to do this isn't about my feelings  my emotions this is about the formulas  of the deal that's the first lesson  second lesson is always be prepared to  walk away just because you've paid a  finest fee just because you paid a  survey just because you are invested  whether that be resources time money  doesn't mean that you have to go ahead  with a deal unless you're buying it from  auction or scotland where the rules are  different but be prepared to walk away  from a deal  third lesson is um prices of materials  have gone up a lot  in the last year or two so factor that  in on your refurb costs due diligence  due diligence due diligence get the  right team and professionals to go out  and look at your properties also know  the area well next lesson know the area  well make sure that you calculate the  gross development value i.e the end  value based on like for like comparables  not comparables quarter of a mile away  that are actually in a better side of  town so i thought i'd share this video  with you for complete transparency so  you can see what i'm doing and i hope  you learned some valuable lessons if you  want to see more videos like this you  can subscribe right up here also there's  a whole playlist of videos of properties  that have gone wrong and things that  haven't worked out so if you want to  learn from my mistakes check out the  playlist right here and i hope you can  join me at the property millionaire  intensive where i'm going to be sharing  how to make money from property not just  buying properties and renting them out  but actually pushing the value up and  then selling them or refinancing them  hope to see you there thanks for  watching

